      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree! I just started introducing world physbone objects into my VRC World projects. I think allowing World Physbones to collide with a chosen collision layer (i.e. \"Walkthrough\") instead of specifically a VRC Physbone Collider gameobject would truly be nice. The plane has a limitation. While box would be fine, but I am worried I would be finding myself tempted to re-set up Physbone box colliders on top of world box colliders and it just feels it could be repetitive. Though this way I could just set up the physbone to work with the already existing walkthrough colliders I have carefully placed in my world and I don't have to redo work. Some are also low poly mesh colliders, and it would also be nice if the holes or curves in those surfaces would be used and respected by the (specifically) world physbone object's collision, too. \n\n(Edit: In my case I would only really want this to function for physbone world objects and not for players' physbones. When gravity is used on the physbone world objects it makes sense to me to also not allow them them clip through the world's colliders for better virtual immersion that the item is like a physical object.)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
